{title: A New Covenant}
{artist: Larry Holder}
{key: Em}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 95}

Verse 1
I will [Em]bring a new covenant, says the [Am]Lord,
With My [D]people, yes, with My [Em]people,
Not as the first one that I made
When I de[Am]livered them out of bondage,
When I [B]led My people [B7]to the Promised [Em]Land.

Verse 2
For the covenant made between us, says the [Am]Lord,
With My [D]people, yes, with My [Em]people,
Has been broken by rebellion
Tho' to [Am]them I was a Husband,
Tho' I de[B]livered them with a [B7]sure and mighty [Em]Hand.

Refrain
This shall I [Am]do, this [D]now I [G]say:
I shall [Am]write upon their [D]hearts a brand new [G]Promise.
They shall a[Am]bide in this new and [D]glorious [G]Way,
With I their [Am]God,
[D]And they My [Em]people.

Verse 3
(Instrumental; repeat refrain; at end add...)
With I their [Am]God,[B]
And [B7]they My [Em]people!
